.TH DTP 1
.SH NAME
dtp \\- detect daemon executable-tree changes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dtp
dtp (--index|--check) --key KEY_FILE [--root DIRECTORY] [--state FILE]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates or compares an HMAC-authenticated daemon baseline. Keys require at least 16 bytes and checks fail closed for unreadable entries.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBdtp --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
